  "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting",
  "@type": "dcs:ContractTemplate",
  "_comment": "Readable @ids on purpose. The builder mints urn:uuid: rule ids and #block-<uuid> prose anchors; the shapes require an IRI, not a particular one, so this BDD fixture uses speaking fragments to stay legible to whoever debugs a failing scenario. Realism is proved elsewhere: the e2e authors through the UI and therefore exercises the real urn:uuid: form. Do not 'fix' these ids. Everything else here is the shape the authoring path emits -- see the header of backend/internal/base/validation/slahostingfixture_test.go. The \"@context\" is a prefix map with no remote IRI, matching the templates every other step module posts (steps/support/services/template_service.py canonical_document_data) -- normalizeCanonicalContext prepends the hub's own served, host-absolute context URL to it (DCS_PUBLIC_URL). Naming https://w3id.org/facis/dcs/context/v1 here instead makes isHubContextAnchor treat the document as already anchored, so normalization returns early, the document keeps an IRI nothing serves, and pdf-core -- which expands over real HTTP rather than through the hub's hermetic loader -- 404s the render. The prefixes must be the hub context's own (enforceCanonicalOntologyIRIs rejects a redefinition).",
  "dcs:contractData": [
    {
      "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#asset-hosting-environment",
      "@type": "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#ManagedKubernetesEnvironment",
      "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#nodeClass": {
        "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#field-node-class"
      },
      "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#provisionedNodes": {
        "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#field-provisioned-nodes"
      },
      "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#serviceRegion": {
        "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#field-service-region"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#asset-support-service",
      "@type": "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#SupportService",
      "https://w3id.org/facis/sla/hosting/v1#incidentResponseMinutes": {
        "@id": "did:web:example:template:sla-hosting#field-incident-response-minutes"
      }
    }
  ],
